ativeness":0.9342852830886841,"text_excerpt":"This spot is a super nice black-owned winery! I came for a mid-day birthday party on a Saturday and it truly was the perfect venue. The winery allowed the party to bring in their own caterer and bottles of liquor, but they provided a super nice charcuterie spread (which I was grateful for because I wasn't veering from keto that day!). Also, the party was allowed to play their own music on a speaker. There was seating inside of the distillery as well as outdoor seating. The outside seating was picnic table style with a view of O.C. Haley; the only improvement I'd recommend is MORE SHADE. The only shade in the outside area are umbrellas at each table so, if the shade isn't casted in your pa..."},{"business_id":"Dd5Spj9DJiXydAy9N3mM5g","review_id":"ZRum6u0dJLFrrKS05V_GxA","date":"2021-02-15T15:43:03","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9209272861480713,"text_excerpt":"Had the pleasure of supporting this BOB within the CBD(central business district) of NOLA. It is located approximately one block from the Mission homeless shelter. The owner and I kind of went back and forth with timing of our experience but my party of 5 remained flexible. It was a great experience! Immediately the vibes were infectious and hospitable. Loved the charcuterie board and the wine tasting. Loved hearing the hostess side Of the history of her business as well as the different wine and what you should pair it with. Impressive. Can't wait to visit again and they're is also a virtual tasting where they mail you items in the mail. How cool!"},{"business_id":"Dd5Spj9DJiXydAy9N3mM5g","review_id":"4m9CCkDD45Yoyb-S3HkZMQ","date":"2021-05-21T23:52:18","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8955146074295044,"text_excerpt":"I was here for a business meeting. Our server was great, the seating outdoors was really nice, full of art, colors k mellow music. I had the flight & loved them all but my favorite was the Rose! Can't wait to return to sip & chill on the 